! `al2-metal.in` with Methfessel-Paxton smearing at degauss=0.04, everything else unchanged.
! A Gaussian-type tail that the Marzari-Vanderbilt smearing of al2-metal.in does not have:
! at QE's projector cutoff (setup_nbnd_occ's small = 6.96e-5) the elastic constants of this
! cell missed a five-point free-energy difference by -4.6e-4, flat in the step, and the strain
! route's own cutoff (STRAIN_SMEARING_SMALL) is what fixed it (notes/incompat/I88.md).
 &control
    calculation='scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=0, celldm(1)=7.50,
    nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=15.0, nosym=.true., noinv=.true.,
    occupations='smearing', smearing='methfessel-paxton', degauss=0.04
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  -0.50  0.00  0.50
   0.00  0.50  0.50
  -1.00  1.00  0.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98 Al.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al  0.00  0.00  0.00
 Al -0.50  0.50  0.00
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 2 0 0 0
